;; fault-selfmod.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-selfmod.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-selfmod.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-selfmod.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-selfmod.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). D-CODE-VISIBILITY: this laboratory re-reads memory on every fetch, so the store that" "patches step 5's word is visible immediately — step 5 executes the PATCHED encoding and writes" "x2 = 7, not 2. The derivation is the laboratory's declared choice (a legal one, not an" "architectural guarantee); MEASURED before authoring: sail-riscv 0.14 AND spike 1.1.1-dev both" "re-read too, so the choice is pinned three-way rather than asserted.")
(expectations (program "fault-selfmod.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 7) (step (n 0) (insn "lui x1, 0x00700") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000700000"))) (derivation "0x00700 << 12 = 0x00700000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "addi x1, x1, 0x113") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000700113"))) (derivation "0x00700000 + 0x113 = 0x00700113, which IS the little-endian encoding of `addi x2, x0, 7` (imm = 7 at bits 31..20, rs1 = 0, funct3 = 0, rd = 2, opcode 0010011) — the patch value, assembled from the encoding rule, never read back from any model.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4; §1.1.2 (the I-format layout)")) (step (n 2) (insn "auipc x3, 0") (writes (write (reg "x3") (value "0x0000000080000008"))) (derivation "AUIPC adds the sign-extended U-immediate (0) to the address OF THIS INSTRUCTION: x3 = 0x80000008 — the current pc, materialized without a hardcoded constant.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-LUI-AUIPC: the offset is added to the address of the AUIPC instruction)")) (step (n 3) (insn "sw x1, 12, x3") (writes) (derivation "The effective address is 0x80000008 + 12 = 0x80000014 — step 5's word. SW stores the low 32 bits of rs2 (0x00700113) there, inside the declared region, aligned: a store writes no register, so the expectation is the empty writes table. The one store crossing of the run is census-pinned.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.3 (D-LOAD-EXT: SW stores the low 32 bits); RVI-RV32I §1.1.6")) (step (n 4) (insn "addi x4, x0, 4") (writes (write (reg "x4") (value "0x0000000000000004"))) (derivation "An ordinary write between the patch and its target.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 5) (insn "addi x2, x0, 2") (writes (write (reg "x2") (value "0x0000000000000007"))) (derivation "⭐ D-CODE-VISIBILITY: the source text says `addi x2, x0, 2`, but step 3's store replaced this word with 0x00700113 = `addi x2, x0, 7`, and this laboratory re-reads memory on every fetch — so the step executes the PATCHED encoding and x2 = 7. A caching model would write 2 and would not be wrong (the base ISA without Zifencei permits it); both pinned references were measured to re-read, so all three observations agree on 7.") (source "RVI-INTRO, Memory (implicit reads; D-CODE-VISIBILITY, the laboratory's declared choice)")) (step (n 6) (insn "addi x5, x0, 5") (writes (write (reg "x5") (value "0x0000000000000005"))) (derivation "The landing.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")))
